Archon — Institutional OTC Settlement Platform

Compliant tokenized fund infrastructure for asset managers, prime brokers, and auditors.
Live on Ethereum Sepolia. Real contracts. Real settlement. Real audit trail.

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

WHAT IS ARCHON

Archon is a bilateral OTC settlement layer for tokenized fund shares. It combines:

  - EIP-712 cryptographic seller consent — trades cannot be proposed without
    a signed authorization from the seller, verified on-chain via ecrecover.

  - Atomic settlement — tokens burn from seller and mint to buyer in a single
    transaction. No partial settlement. No intermediate custody.

  - Programmable compliance — KYC eligibility, AML velocity limits, and NAV
    floors enforced by smart contracts and API middleware before any transaction
    reaches the chain.

  - Permissionless auditability — every NAV post, trade, mint, and burn is
    permanently recorded on Ethereum. Any auditor with an RPC endpoint can
    independently verify the full fund history.

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

DEPLOYED CONTRACTS (Ethereum Sepolia)

  FundToken (ERC-20)   — Whitelist-gated fund shares with subscription and
                          redemption roles. Transfer hook enforces KYC on all
                          token movements.

  NAVRegistry          — On-chain NAV oracle. Authenticated posts with
                          timestamps, queryable by OTCTrade at settlement.

  OTCTrade             — Bilateral settlement engine. Requires SETTLEMENT_AGENT_ROLE
                          to propose, EIP-712 seller signature to authorize,
                          and passes 5 on-chain checks before settlement:
                          seller balance, NAV floor, NAV freshness (24h),
                          trade expiry (7 days), and signature validity.

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

QUICKSTART (Docker — recommended)

  Prerequisites: Docker + Docker Compose

  1. Copy and fill environment files:

       cp apps/api/.env.example apps/api/.env
       cp apps/web/.env.example apps/web/.env.local

  2. Start all services:

       docker compose up --build

  3. Open the platform:

       http://localhost:3000

  Demo login credentials (hardcoded for beta):

    Role           Username    Password
    ─────────────  ──────────  ────────────
    Investor       investor    investor123
    Fund Manager   manager     manager123
    Auditor        auditor     auditor123

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

QUICKSTART (Local dev — Anvil)

  Prerequisites: Node.js ≥ 20, pnpm, Foundry (forge + anvil)

  Install Foundry:
    curl -L https://foundry.paradigm.xyz | bash && foundryup

  Run everything in one command:
    ./start.sh

  This starts Anvil, deploys contracts, seeds test accounts, starts the API
  and web UI. All contract addresses and API keys are auto-generated.

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

SYSTEM ARCHITECTURE

  ┌─────────────────────┐     ┌──────────────────────┐     ┌──────────────┐
  │   Web UI (Next.js)  │────▶│   API (Fastify/TS)   │────▶│  Contracts   │
  │   localhost:3000    │     │   localhost:3001      │     │  (Solidity)  │
  └─────────────────────┘     └──────────────────────┘     └──────────────┘
           │                            │                         │
           │  JWT sessions              │  X-Api-Key auth         │  Ethereum
           │  Role-gated pages          │  KYC/AML/Sanctions      │  Sepolia /
           │  EIP-712 signing           │  NAV scheduler          │  Anvil (dev)
           └────────────────────────────┴─────────────────────────┘

  apps/
    api/      Node.js + TypeScript API — chain interaction, KYC, AML, audit
    web/      Next.js frontend — public site, login portal, role-based dashboards
  contracts/  Solidity (Foundry) — FundToken, NAVRegistry, OTCTrade

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

PORTALS

  Public (no login required)
    /             Live dashboard — NAV, AUM, OTC feed from Sepolia
    /about        Platform origin and values
    /why-onchain  On-chain vs traditional OTC vs Coinbase Prime
    /platform     Five-step settlement walkthrough
    /contact      Request access form

  Authenticated
    /investor     Token balance, subscribe, redeem          [investor, manager]
    /manager      Post NAV, monitor fund                    [manager]
    /auditor      Download on-chain audit CSV               [auditor, manager]
    /market       Live ETH/BTC market data                  [all roles]
    /otc          Run live OTC settlement scenarios          [manager]

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

KEY API ENDPOINTS

  GET  /health                   Liveness check
  GET  /nav/latest               Latest on-chain NAV
  GET  /token/supply             Total OTCF token supply
  GET  /token/balance/:address   Token balance for an address
  GET  /otc/trades               All trades (Pending / Settled / Cancelled)
  GET  /risk                     Current fund risk status
  GET  /market/prices            Live ETH/BTC prices

  POST /token/subscribe          Mint (KYC + AML checked)        [API key]
  POST /token/redeem             Burn (KYC + AML checked)        [API key]
  POST /nav/post                 Post NAV on-chain               [API key]
  POST /otc/sign-propose         Generate EIP-712 seller consent [API key]
  POST /otc/propose              Submit trade proposal           [API key]
  POST /otc/settle               Settle a pending trade          [API key]
  POST /otc/cancel               Cancel a pending trade          [API key]
  POST /kyc/mark-eligible        Mark address KYC-eligible       [API key]
  GET  /audit/export             Download audit CSV              [API key]

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES

  See apps/api/.env.example and apps/web/.env.example for full documentation.

  Required for production (API):
    RPC_URL, PRIVATE_KEY, FUND_TOKEN_ADDRESS, NAV_REGISTRY_ADDRESS,
    OTC_TRADE_ADDRESS, API_KEY, CORS_ORIGIN

  Strongly recommended for production:
    DATABASE_URL    (PostgreSQL — KYC/AML data persisted across restarts)

  Optional:
    SANCTIONS_API_URL, SANCTIONS_API_KEY, AML_MAX_TX, AML_VELOCITY_24H

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

RESETTING LOCAL STATE

  Stop all processes (Ctrl+C in the start.sh terminal), then re-run:

    ./start.sh

  Note: transactions on Sepolia testnet are permanent and cannot be reverted.
  Resetting only affects the local Anvil dev environment.

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

TROUBLESHOOTING

  forge/anvil not found
    export PATH="$HOME/.foundry/bin:$PATH"

  API won't start — address parse failed
    Check that forge script output contains FundToken/NAVRegistry/OTCTrade
    lines. Re-run ./start.sh.

  Web shows stale data
    The NAV scheduler posts every 60s. Wait one cycle or POST /nav/post manually
    via the Manager portal.

  Docker build fails
    Ensure Docker Desktop is running and you have sufficient disk space (build
    requires ~2 GB).
